            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this description reasonable?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yikai Tsai",
                        "email": "yikai.tsai.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "yikaitsaiww"
                    },
                    "message": "How about \"The IANA number for the device\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "It sounds more sensible, but I only have the public spec at hand and it doesn't mention IANA at all. How is it used?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yikai Tsai",
                        "email": "yikai.tsai.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "yikaitsaiww"
                    },
                    "message": "IANA is used to implement custom OEM features for some projects. In our case, we used IANA to check if OEM events are from Meta devices."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do you need that information in the EM config?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yikai Tsai",
                        "email": "yikai.tsai.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "yikaitsaiww"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not sure if I've misunderstood. Are you suggesting that there might be a more suitable place to store IANA data? If so, could you please provide some suggestions?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not suggesting there's a more appropriate place, I'm trying to understand how you're using it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yikai Tsai",
                        "email": "yikai.tsai.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "yikaitsaiww"
                    },
                    "message": "We implemented a `checkMetaIana` function as a [patch file](https://github.com/facebook/openbmc/blob/helium/common/lfopenbmc/recipes-phosphor/pldm/files/0004-platform-mc-Add-OEM-Meta-event-handler.patch#L961-L976) in pldm that uses the stored IANA info to validate devices, checking if a given  EID corresponds to a Meta device. \nLet me know if you need any further clarification. Thank you!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/mctp.json",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yikai Tsai",
                        "email": "yikai.tsai.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "yikaitsaiww"
                    },
                    "message": "We've removed IANA and decided to use patches to address the IANA usage in our project. Thanks for the discussion."
                }
            ],
